# NO NORTH — THE RIFT.
#
# The brief is the hero's own first line in there: NO FLOOR. NO SKY. NO NORTH.
# MY BOOTS GRIP SOMETHING ANYWAY. A hallucinatory space between universes where
# everyone who ever vanished without a body fell in and is still going about
# their business — a magician, an inventor, an aviator, a lighthouse keeper two
# men short since 1900 — and at the far end a monolith with one enormous eye
# that read everything ever written and told precisely nobody.
#
# THREE DECISIONS, and all three are the same sentence said three ways.
#
#   NO TONIC. Every chord in the track is AUGMENTED or SUSPENDED and there is
#   not one major or minor triad in it anywhere. An augmented triad cuts the
#   octave into three equal pieces, so no note in it is the root and the ear
#   has nothing to stand on; a suspended chord is a chord that has not decided.
#   The piece never states a key and never resolves, including at the seam.
#
#   SOMETHING IS ALWAYS FALLING. Two voices descend by semitones at DIFFERENT
#   RATES — one an octave over eight bars, the other over four — so their
#   restarts never coincide and at every moment of the track at least one line
#   is halfway down. Nothing catches either of them.
#
#   THE BAR LIMPS. Everything that strikes, strikes at 3+3+3+3+4 rather than
#   4+4+4+4: four short steps and then one that is one too long, every bar, for
#   two minutes. The count never comes out and the ear keeps starting again.
#   Only the drifting lead is free of it, which is why it sounds untethered
#   rather than merely slow.
#
# Compile:  node scripts/song-import.mjs content/songs/rift_drift.song --sheet

id     rift_drift
title  NO NORTH
tempo  88
about
  Weightless and homeless on purpose. There is no major or minor chord
  anywhere in this score — only augmented triads, which divide the octave into
  three equal parts so that no note in them is the root, and suspended chords,
  which are chords that have not decided. Two lines fall by semitones at
  different rates, one an octave every eight bars and one every four, so their
  restarts never line up and something is always partway down. And everything
  that strikes, strikes at 3+3+3+3+4 — four short steps and one that is one too
  long — so the bar never comes out even; only the drifting sine is free of the
  count, which is what makes it sound untethered rather than slow. Original
  melodies; nothing sampled.

# ── THE CAST ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The one voice with no meter and no floor. Long, bent, drowned in echo.
voice drift  sine vol=.03 gate=.9 attack=200 echo=.6 vib=3.5/26/300
# THE TWO FALLS. Same patch, opposite sides of the field, different rates.
voice fallA  square vol=.012 gate=.9 attack=120 detune=10 pan=-0.35 echo=.5
voice fallB  square vol=.012 gate=.9 attack=120 detune=10 pan=.35 echo=.5
# Glass — high, sparse, and it answers nothing.
voice glass  sine vol=.014 gate=.25 pan=.4 echo=.55
# A heartbeat heard through a wall. It limps with everything else.
voice deep   triangle vol=.05 gate=.6

# ── THE KIT, WHICH MOSTLY DECLINES ─────────────────────────────────────────
drum tom     triangle vol=.03 gate=1 slide=.3 note=A1
drum shake   noise vol=.0085 gate=.18 hp=7600 pan=-0.2

# ── OPEN — a step through, and the falling has already been going on ───────
section open
  chords Aaug | Aaug | Csus2 | Csus2
  fallA  c6*3 c6*3 c6*3 c6*3 c6*4 | b5*3 b5*3 b5*3 b5*3 b5*4
         a#5*3 a#5*3 a#5*3 a#5*3 a#5*4 | a5*3 a5*3 a5*3 a5*3 a5*4
  drift  .*16 | .*16 | a5*8 c#6*8 | f6*8 .*8
  deep   .*16 | .*16 | a2*3 a2*3 a2*3 a2*3 a2*4 | a2*3 a2*3 a2*3 a2*3 a2*4
  shake  ................|................|..x..x..x..x..x.|..x..x..x..x..x.

# ── A — nothing here is a key ──────────────────────────────────────────────
section a
  chords Aaug | Aaug | Csus2 | Csus2 | Caug | Caug | Fsus2 | Fsus2
  drift  a5*8 c#6*8 | f6*8 c#6*8 | d6*8 g5*8 | c6*8 c6*8
         g#5*8 e5*8 | c6*8 g#5*8 | g5*8 c6*8 | f5*8 .*8
  fallA  c6*3 c6*3 c6*3 c6*3 c6*4 | b5*3 b5*3 b5*3 b5*3 b5*4
         a#5*3 a#5*3 a#5*3 a#5*3 a#5*4 | a5*3 a5*3 a5*3 a5*3 a5*4
         g#5*3 g#5*3 g#5*3 g#5*3 g#5*4 | g5*3 g5*3 g5*3 g5*3 g5*4
         f#5*3 f#5*3 f#5*3 f#5*3 f#5*4 | f5*3 f5*3 f5*3 f5*3 f5*4
  fallB  f#5*3 f#5*3 f5*3 f5*3 f5*4 | e5*3 e5*3 d#5*3 d#5*3 d#5*4
         d5*3 d5*3 c#5*3 c#5*3 c#5*4 | c5*3 c5*3 b4*3 b4*3 b4*4
  deep   a2*3 a2*3 a2*3 a2*3 a2*4 | a2*3 a2*3 a2*3 a2*3 a2*4
         c2*3 c2*3 c2*3 c2*3 c2*4 | c2*3 c2*3 c2*3 c2*3 c2*4
         c2*3 c2*3 c2*3 c2*3 c2*4 | c2*3 c2*3 c2*3 c2*3 c2*4
         f2*3 f2*3 f2*3 f2*3 f2*4 | f2*3 f2*3 f2*3 f2*3 f2*4
  tom    x........x......
  shake  ..x..x..x..x..x.

# ── B — the same nowhere, wider, with something ringing overhead ───────────
section b
  chords Dsus2 | Faug | Gsus4 | Bbaug | Csus2 | Eaug | Fsus2 | Aaug
  drift  e6*8 a5*8 | a5*8 c#6*8 | d6*8 g5*8 | f#6*8 d6*8
         g5*8 d6*8 | g#5*8 c6*8 | c6*8 f5*8 | a5*8 c#6*8
  glass  arp16 6
  fallA  c6*3 c6*3 c6*3 c6*3 c6*4 | b5*3 b5*3 b5*3 b5*3 b5*4
         a#5*3 a#5*3 a#5*3 a#5*3 a#5*4 | a5*3 a5*3 a5*3 a5*3 a5*4
         g#5*3 g#5*3 g#5*3 g#5*3 g#5*4 | g5*3 g5*3 g5*3 g5*3 g5*4
         f#5*3 f#5*3 f#5*3 f#5*3 f#5*4 | f5*3 f5*3 f5*3 f5*3 f5*4
  fallB  f#5*3 f#5*3 f5*3 f5*3 f5*4 | e5*3 e5*3 d#5*3 d#5*3 d#5*4
         d5*3 d5*3 c#5*3 c#5*3 c#5*4 | c5*3 c5*3 b4*3 b4*3 b4*4
  deep   d2*3 d2*3 d2*3 d2*3 d2*4 | f2*3 f2*3 f2*3 f2*3 f2*4
         g2*3 g2*3 g2*3 g2*3 g2*4 | a#2*3 a#2*3 a#2*3 a#2*3 a#2*4
         c2*3 c2*3 c2*3 c2*3 c2*4 | e2*3 e2*3 e2*3 e2*3 e2*4
         f2*3 f2*3 f2*3 f2*3 f2*4 | a2*3 a2*3 a2*3 a2*3 a2*4
  tom    x........x......
  shake  ..x..x..x..x..x.

# ── EYE — the monolith. One chord for four bars, then another. It read
#    everything ever written about you and it is not going to say so ────────
section eye
  chords Eaug | Eaug | Eaug | Eaug | Caug | Caug | Caug | Caug
  drift  e5*8 g#5*8 | c6*8 g#5*8 | e5*8 c6*8 | g#5*16
         c6*8 e6*8 | g#5*8 e5*8 | c6*8 g#5*8 | e5*16
  glass  c7*4 .*12 | .*16 | .*7 g#6*4 .*5 | .*16
  fallB  f#5*3 f#5*3 f5*3 f5*3 f5*4 | e5*3 e5*3 d#5*3 d#5*3 d#5*4
         d5*3 d5*3 c#5*3 c#5*3 c#5*4 | c5*3 c5*3 b4*3 b4*3 b4*4
  deep   e2*3 e2*3 e2*3 e2*3 e2*4 | .*16 | e2*3 e2*3 e2*3 e2*3 e2*4 | .*16
         c2*3 c2*3 c2*3 c2*3 c2*4 | .*16 | c2*3 c2*3 c2*3 c2*3 c2*4 | .*16

# ── CLOSE — one line still going down, and the seam is not a cadence ───────
section close
  chords Fsus2 | Fsus2 | Aaug | Aaug
  drift  f5*8 c6*8 | g5*8 .*8 | c#6*8 a5*8 | .*16
  fallA  g#5*3 g#5*3 g#5*3 g#5*3 g#5*4 | g5*3 g5*3 g5*3 g5*3 g5*4
         f#5*3 f#5*3 f#5*3 f#5*3 f#5*4 | f5*3 f5*3 f5*3 f5*3 f5*4
  deep   f2*3 f2*3 f2*3 f2*3 f2*4 | f2*3 f2*3 f2*3 f2*3 f2*4
         a2*3 a2*3 a2*3 a2*3 a2*4 | .*16
  shake  ..x..x..x..x..x.|..x..x..x..x..x.|..x..x..x..x..x.|................

order  open a b a eye b close
